statement:
Let P, j ∈ ℕ and let C ∈ 𝒟_j(ℝ^P) (GeometricCurrentOn univ j) be a cone, i.e. IsConeCurrent C: currentEval(η_{0,λ#}C)(ω) = C(ω) for every λ > 0 and every test form ω ∈ 𝒟^j(ℝ^P), where η_{0,λ#}C = blowUp C 0 λ. Assume C has integer multiplicity, i.e. IsIntegerMultiplicity C: C = τ(M, θ, ξ) for some integer multiplicity triple R in ℝ^P (R.Represents C). Write M_W(C) = C.massOn W ∈ [0, ∞] and ω_j := unitBallVolume j, the Lebesgue measure of the open unit ball of ℝ^j. Then:
(i) M_{B_ρ(0)}(C) = ofReal(ρ^j)·M_{B_1(0)}(C) for every real ρ > 0 (open balls);
(ii) for every real θ, HasMassDensity C 0 θ holds iff θ ≥ 0 and M_{B_1(0)}(C) = ω_j·ofReal(θ);
(iii) for every real θ > 0, HasMassDensity C 0 θ implies 0 ∈ spt C (C.support).
No minimality and no restriction on j are assumed.
